# 10km loop settings, sourced as shell. An environment variable of the same name
# overrides a setting. Scripts read the copy in the central loop worktree, so
# changes take effect once a Curator has merged them into main. Repos are
# configured in their own git config (prompts/kickoff.md).

# State database, action log and usage log. Empty: <LOOP_ROOT>/.10km/loop.db,
# with actions.log and usage.jsonl next to it.
MSM_DB="${MSM_DB-}"
MSM_LOG="${MSM_LOG-}"
USAGE_LOG="${USAGE_LOG-}"

# Seconds between Dispatcher passes (run-loop).
DISPATCH_INTERVAL="${DISPATCH_INTERVAL-60}"
# Session time-out in seconds; per role: PLANNER_TIMEOUT, WORKER_TIMEOUT,
# CURATOR_TIMEOUT, AUDITOR_TIMEOUT.
SESSION_TIMEOUT="${SESSION_TIMEOUT-3600}"
# Seconds between SIGTERM and SIGKILL when stopping an agent.
KILL_GRACE="${KILL_GRACE-10}"
# Seconds after launch before a session that doesn't look alive is expired.
START_GRACE="${START_GRACE-180}"
MAX_WORKERS="${MAX_WORKERS-4}"
# Open backlog size at which the Planner must prioritise or prune.
BACKLOG_SIZE="${BACKLOG_SIZE-50}"

# The Auditor is due daily after AUDIT_TIME (HH:MM) in AUDIT_TIMEZONE, or after
# AUDIT_CYCLES_LIMIT curated cycles. Empty or 0 disables a trigger.
AUDIT_TIME="${AUDIT_TIME-07:00}"
AUDIT_TIMEZONE="${AUDIT_TIMEZONE-UTC}"
AUDIT_CYCLES_LIMIT="${AUDIT_CYCLES_LIMIT-0}"

# Consecutive empty cycles after which the Curator stops the loop as idle.
IDLE_CYCLE_LIMIT="${IDLE_CYCLE_LIMIT-3}"

# Gates: one command per line, or `repo: command`; non-zero exit fails. Workers
# run WORKER_GATES before done, the Curator VALIDATION_GATES.
WORKER_GATES="${WORKER_GATES-}"
VALIDATION_GATES="${VALIDATION_GATES-}"
# Seconds `gate` waits before exiting 3 (rerun to wait). Keep it under the
# agent's tool-call limit (Claude Code: 10 minutes).
GATE_WAIT="${GATE_WAIT-540}"

# Notification commands, one per line, run with TENKM_PRIORITY, TENKM_TITLE,
# TENKM_BODY and TENKM_PROJECT set. Empty: append to NOTIFICATIONS.md.
NOTIFY_CMD="${NOTIFY_CMD-}"

# The process launcher runs LOOP_AGENT, or PLANNER_AGENT, WORKER_AGENT,
# CURATOR_AGENT or AUDITOR_AGENT for that role, in the session directory with
# SESSION, PROMPT_FILE and FIRST_MESSAGE set. Usage figures reach USAGE_LOG only
# from harnesses that print them: Claude Code with --output-format json (tokens,
# cost), kiro-cli with --output-format stream-json (credits, time; its default
# text output reports none).
LAUNCHER="${LAUNCHER-process}"
[ -n "${LOOP_AGENT+x}" ] || LOOP_AGENT='claude --no-session-persistence --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format json -n "$SESSION" -p "$FIRST_MESSAGE"'
# LOOP_AGENT='codex exec "$FIRST_MESSAGE"'
# LOOP_AGENT='kiro-cli chat --no-interactive --output-format stream-json --trust-all-tools "$FIRST_MESSAGE"'

# The operator's agent, for kickoff and operator sessions; it doesn't fall back
# to LOOP_AGENT. It runs with FIRST_MESSAGE (empty for a plain session), SESSION
# (not for kickoff) and ONE_SHOT=1 for a one-shot instruction.
[ -n "${OPERATOR_AGENT+x}" ] || OPERATOR_AGENT='claude ${SESSION:+-n "$SESSION"} ${ONE_SHOT:+-p} ${FIRST_MESSAGE:+"$FIRST_MESSAGE"}'
